  "title": "Exclude earlier caches at every owned P104 MOVE and all public cuts with a live source reconstruction",
  "body": "## Exact scoped result\n\nExclude earlier destination-cache reconstruction at **every one of the 47 owned\nMOVEs** in the exact #7481 native, and at **all 18 public cuts with a live source\nreconstruction**. These are 65 distinct cuts. The owned result has no live-source\npremise: deferred source cleanup cannot fix the missing destination value.\n\nAll 1,501 public inputs remain arbitrary. The screen pools every strictly earlier\ncoframed native observation, so it grants an arbitrary finite collection of\nzero-initialized ordinary linear caches, preparation, storage and cleanup free.\n**No new kappa** or unconditional multiplication theorem is claimed.\n\n## Novelty, pins and evidence\n\n#7308 checks live destination banks at the 47 owned clocks on #7277. #6069 treats\nan older #6030 word: 4,033 leaking injection classes including dynamic affine\nclosure, 764 incoming-only intervals, and five private rank-four output seams.\nThis contribution credits those actual scopes and adds the complete later-word\ncumulative-history test and the temporal owned extension.\n\nCanonical base: `e54523517d0f03e58352e647c403a5af3e525a57`.\nExact unselected #7481 head: `89eaa9d8cae37c1540de98f2d29a3abaabb96a2b`.\nOriginal paths, blobs and SHA256 pins are in `SOURCES.json`; scientific input\nbytes are bundled.\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-earlier-destination-cache-bound\n```\n\nExpected status: `PASS_P104_EARLIER_DESTINATION_CACHE_EXCLUSION`.\nThe complete exact relation-kernel census covers all 6,279 MOVEs. Two distinct\nrational history engines check all 49 live-source survivors, their exact witnesses\nand history ranks. Two temporal replays cover the additional 16 owned cuts and\nindependently replay all 47 owned cuts. The latter finds exactly 31 genuine\nlater-source memberships, providing positive controls. Every one of the 76,475\ninstructions is replayed. Source-byte mutations, inserted-arrival controls and\n44 independent synthetic donor queries detect false acceptance and rejection.\nNormal, optimized and read-only Git-free export checks are in `VALIDATION.json`.\n\n## Limits and credit\n\nThe history and public input space are unchanged. Helper restrictions or\ncorrelations, incoming transported stock, changed earlier native operations,\nother nonlinear mechanisms and a complete physical supplier remain open.\nAll five foundational assumptions remain. No selected certificate is changed.\n\nPrepared for **Jerry Chen / @CubeJerry** with substantial **OpenAI assistance**\nin research, separate exact implementations, review and packaging. Retain\nClear1nsight #7481 and its lineage, ToikY #7308, Jonathan Capalbo #6069 and all\noriginal notices. No independent human or proof-kernel acceptance is claimed.\nThe complete proof and open questions are in the package.\n\n[Complete package description](https://github.com/CubeJerry/integer-mult-bounds/blob/1c741b71275f58c6b5ad5e00f73b53423e6c7910/research/p104-earlier-destination-cache-bound/PR-DESCRIPTION.md).\n",
